## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to architect privacy-aware computer vision systems under strict edge constraints while balancing accuracy and privacy guarantees. Requires concrete architecture, differentiable privacy terms, and rigorous evaluation plans.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving CV and de-identification modules
- Differentiable privacy loss and threat-model-aware evaluation
- Edge/on-device inference and latency budgeting
- Trade-offs between detection accuracy and privacy guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight total loss combining detection accuracy and privacy
function computeTotalLoss(detectionPred, privacyPred, targets) {
    const detectionLoss = computeDetectionLoss(detectionPred, targets);
    const privacyLoss = computePrivacyLoss(privacyPred, targets.sensitiveRegions);

    // Weighted combination with privacy budget constraint
    return detectionLoss + lambdaPrivacy * privacyLoss;
}

// Differentiable de-identification module
class PrivacyModule {
    obfuscate(features, sensitiveRegions) {
        // Apply learnable obfuscation to sensitive regions
        return features.map((feat, i) => 
            sensitiveRegions[i] ? this.anonymize(feat) : feat
        );
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design end-to-end computer vision systems that fuse perception with physics for deformable objects in cluttered environments, while also demonstrating expertise in efficient on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- On-device few-shot adaptation
- 2.5D depth and surface normals representation
- Differentiable physics for stiffness estimation
- Grasp affordance learning with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: training loop for temporally-consistent affordance learning
for (batch of data) {
  const pred = model.forward(images);
  const affordanceLoss = computeBCE(pred.heatmap, target.heatmap);
  const depthLoss = computeL1(pred.depth, target.depth);
  const physicsLoss = computePhysicsConsistency(pred.stiffness, pred.depth);

  const totalLoss = affordanceLoss + depthLoss + physicsLoss;
  optimizer.step(totalLoss);
}

